#
# The core's configuration at Latere; every TOPOS_* variable is in the
# core's configuration reference (topos docs/configuration.md). The bearers
# are the Secret toposd, the database URLs the Secret topos-core-db,
# and the host client's secret the Secret toposd-identity, each named in the
# Deployment patch; none of them is here.
#
# The origin serves the core under /v1/agents, and the core serves
# its API under that base path in the place of its own /v1 (topos spec 030),
# so the Ingress forwards without a rewrite: the agent collection is
# /v1/agents/agents, a session /v1/agents/sessions/{id}, and the document
# /v1/agents/openapi.yaml. The base path is the public URL's path, and the
# core refuses to start when the two differ. The public URL is the base of
# every URL an answer writes, a session's stream Link among them.
TOPOS_PUBLIC_URL=https://api.latere.ai/v1/agents
TOPOS_BASE_PATH=/v1/agents
TOPOS_OIDC_ISSUERS=https://auth.latere.ai
# The core's data directory. On Postgres it holds nothing a replica keeps
# past a send: a file a message brings is spooled to it while it is copied
# into the conversation, at most 2 GiB at once, and removed when the send
# ends. The root filesystem is read only, so it is the emptyDir the
# Deployment patch mounts here.
TOPOS_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/topos
# platformd's internal TLS listener: the Topos decider every API action is
# asked of, and the session key routes, which append /{session}/keys/{workload}
# to this URL and register each session's Lux keys by hash.
TOPOS_AUTHORIZER_URL=https://platformd-internal.latere.svc.cluster.local/internal/topos/authorize
# Auto picks a level by what a message asks so a
# person's message may reach the authorizer in words: only on a session
# whose last allow named message_text, which platformd names only while
# a decision model is chosen, and only the message's opening.
TOPOS_AUTHORIZER_MESSAGE_TEXT=true
TOPOS_SESSION_KEYS_URL=https://platformd-internal.latere.svc.cluster.local/internal/topos/sessions
# platformd's web search route on the same listener: a session's web_search
# call goes there with the session's own Key, and platformd charges the
# wallet the session's Keys draw and calls the search provider. With session
# keys the core needs no TOPOS_SEARCH_KEY.
TOPOS_SEARCH_URL=https://platformd-internal.latere.svc.cluster.local/internal/topos/search
# auth hosts the agents applied here: each agent is an
# identity created at its first apply, and each session reaches Cella with
# minutes-long tokens auth mints for it. topos-service is the host client of
# auth's registry; its secret is the file the Deployment mounts from
# toposd-identity.
TOPOS_IDENTITY_URL=https://auth.latere.ai
TOPOS_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID=topos-service
TOPOS_IDENTITY_SECRET_FILE=/var/run/toposd-identity/client-secret
# The Lux core at its Service in the cluster, under the prefix it serves
# at. The core reads Lux's discovery document here and reaches each door it
# names under this root, so no model request leaves the cluster. A sandbox
# reaches Lux at the root the document publishes its doors under,
# https://api.latere.ai/v1/models, the only kind of address its egress
# gateway reaches; that is its LUX_URL, and its Lux key is swapped in on
# requests to that host.
TOPOS_MODELS_URL=http://luxd-core.latere.svc.cluster.local:8080/v1/models
# The Cella core in the cluster, under the prefix it serves at: the Cella
# client puts this path in the place of /v1, so a sandbox is
# /v1/environments/sandboxes/{id} on the cellad Service.
TOPOS_CELLA_URL=http://cellad.latere.svc.cluster.local/v1/environments
# The cellad Service answers plain http:// inside the cluster, which the
# Cella client refuses on a host other than loopback without this explicit
# consent (topos v0.67.0 refuses to start without it). In-cluster TLS for
# cellad would remove it.
TOPOS_CELLA_INSECURE=true
# Origo's git host, which a session's sandbox clones from and pushes to
# with its agent's token: the sandbox holds a placeholder that Cella's
# egress gateway swaps for the token on requests to this host, and the host
# joins the sandbox's egress allowlist with the Secret. The sandbox reaches
# it through the gateway, never through toposd, so the core's own egress
# names nothing for it.
TOPOS_ORIGO_URL=https://code.latere.ai
# The app host a session publishes a folder to with the publish tool: Apps
# at its public origin, which the core reaches through the ingress
# controller as it reaches auth, with the session's own token for the
# audience insula, which auth mints for topos-service. An app's repository
# is on TOPOS_ORIGO_URL's host, where the sandbox pushes the folder.
TOPOS_APPS_URL=https://api.latere.ai/v1/apps
TOPOS_APPS_AUDIENCE=insula
# The parsing service read sends a PDF of a session's folder to: Parsing
# at its public origin, which the core reaches through the ingress
# controller as it reaches Apps, with the session's own token for the
# audience lectio, which auth mints for topos-service. platformd decides
# the session's parse as its initiator, of a file in its own folder.
# v0.44.0 is the first release that reads it.
TOPOS_PARSING_URL=https://api.latere.ai/v1/parsing
# The connection service, Pons at Connections' public origin (topos spec
# 069): every sandbox mounts a Secret holding the session's
# token for the audience pons, scoped to this host, and a connection the
# allow names is reached at its addresses here, git's included, through
# Cella's egress gateway; the runner reaches a connection of kind mcp
# through the ingress controller, as it reaches auth. v0.34.0 is the first
# release that reads both.
#
# TOPOS_CONNECTIONS_URL is the connection service's own host,
# connect.latere.ai, never api.latere.ai: every sandbox mounts a Secret
# scoped to it, and the Lux key's Secret is scoped to api.latere.ai, since a
# sandbox reaches the models at https://api.latere.ai/v1/models. Cella
# refuses a sandbox whose two Secrets are scoped to one host; setting it on
# api.latere.ai on 2026-10-13 refused every hosted session's machine
# (secret_host_conflict) for about 40 minutes.
TOPOS_CONNECTIONS_URL=https://connect.latere.ai/v1/connections
TOPOS_CONNECTIONS_AUDIENCE=pons
# A conversation's files are kept in Storage, in the folder platformd's
# allow names for each session, at the url it names, platformd's
# PLATFORM_ARCA_URL. The core reaches it with tokens for this audience:
# the session's own for its writes and a fork's copy, topos-service's own
# for reading a file back. Storage answers a read with a redirect to the
# object store and takes a large upload's parts there directly, which the
# egress policy admits.
TOPOS_FILES_AUDIENCE=arca
# Sessions each serve replica drives at once. The runners run in the serve
# role, so two replicas drive eight; the runner role's own Deployment is not
# part of this tree.
TOPOS_RUNNER_CAPACITY=4
# The decision service, Limen, the Service limend of latere-ai/limen in this
# namespace (topos specs 037 and 099). toposd sends it each call it decides
# and each answer of the person, and reaches it with topos-service's token
# for TOPOS_DECISIONS_AUDIENCE, which serve requires beside
# TOPOS_IDENTITY_URL once the URL is set.
TOPOS_DECISIONS_URL=http://limend.latere.svc.cluster.local:7720
TOPOS_DECISIONS_AUDIENCE=limen
# Decided 2026-11-01, from topos v0.66.0: in progressive mode, Limen decides a
# call that the rules leave open where it has evidence about the person (its
# allow, its block, and an ask when its evidence leaves the approval
# probability between the thresholds, for example when the answers
# disagree), and the rules and
# the risk score decide where it has too few answers or does not answer, so
# a call waits at most two seconds for it. In confirm mode the rules decide
# and Limen only learns; in plan mode toposd does not ask it. Roll back with TOPOS_DECISIONS_MODE=shadow,
# where the rules and the risk score decide every call and Limen's
# suggestion is only recorded. TOPOS_DECISIONS_SHADOW is the old name of
# shadow, which toposd refuses beside this variable; never set it.
TOPOS_DECISIONS_MODE=learned
# Decided 2026-11-02, from topos v0.68.0: a call of an agent that an organization owns is keyed by the
# organization's id, so the organization's trust profile applies to it and
# Oversight in the organization shows it; a call of a person's own agent,
# Latere Chat's included, stays keyed by the person. A person's answers stay
# theirs in either context. Roll back with TOPOS_DECISIONS_ORG=initiator.
TOPOS_DECISIONS_ORG=agent
